      "status": "blocked",
      "blockedReason": "Both remaining tokens sit on one element, the mobile drawer aside at apps/platform/src/views/okou-page/sidebar.tsx, and draining them needs a design decision about where this shape belongs. okou-mobile-sidebar is isolation isolate plus a six-declaration ::before paint layer plus a standalone-only bottom extension on that layer; okou-mobile-fixed-safe-area is box-sizing and a four-value safe-area padding inside max-width 767px. Spelled as utilities on the consumer that is isolate, before:pointer-events-none, before:absolute, before:inset-0, before:-z-1, before:bg-sidebar, before:content-[\"\"], before:[@media(display-mode:standalone)]:bottom-[calc(-1*var(--sab))], max-md:box-border and max-md:p-[var(--sat)_var(--sar)_var(--sab)_var(--sal)]. Measured, that takes the element from 288 to 499 characters of class list and from 2 to 6 bracketed arbitrary values, four of them new. The element already carried a 235-character single string before any change. Whether that belongs inline, behind a shared safe-area padding decision, or inside a drawer-surface component is a design call about the token layer, not a mechanical substitution, so no value was chosen here. The mechanics are otherwise clear and unblocked: both legacy rules are unlayered, nothing else on the element sets isolation, ::before, padding or box-sizing, so the utilities would not have to outrank anything and no important marker is needed. max-md is also not an exact restatement of the retired condition. Tailwind emits @media (width < 48rem), so between 767px and 768px of viewport width the padding would newly apply while the retired rule stopped at 767px; the element already gates its whole fixed-drawer geometry on max-md, so the two spellings disagree there today. Nothing about this batch depends on data-desktop-shell, so it is independent of the desktop-titlebar block in the same family.",
